From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:19:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Soloud::mixBus_internal: resampled voices no longer drift
 ahead (#314)

When a source block ran out, the check meant to keep the resampler inside
the block tested the frame after the last one to be written, so it always
dropped a frame. Unless the rest of the block was a whole number of steps,
the dropped frame still belonged to that block, and the next block, finding
the playhead short of it, started at its first sample: up to one step of
source was skipped every 512 frames. A 44.1 kHz sound on a 48 kHz engine
played about 0.09% fast, 0.1 s in three minutes as reported in #314. The
check now tests the last frame written, in the mixing and the inaudible
ticking paths.
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index c7927a7..058f405 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -1792,8 +1792,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 					{
 						writesamples = ((SAMPLE_GRANULARITY * FIXPOINT_FRAC_MUL) - voice->mSrcOffset) / step_fixed + 1;
 
-						// avoid reading past the current buffer..
-						if (((writesamples * step_fixed + voice->mSrcOffset) >> FIXPOINT_FRAC_BITS) >= SAMPLE_GRANULARITY)
+						// avoid reading past the current buffer: drop the last frame
+						// only when it lands on the next block's first sample
+						if ((((writesamples - 1) * step_fixed + voice->mSrcOffset) >> FIXPOINT_FRAC_BITS) >= SAMPLE_GRANULARITY)
 							writesamples--;
 					}
 
@@ -1959,8 +1960,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 					{
 						writesamples = ((SAMPLE_GRANULARITY * FIXPOINT_FRAC_MUL) - voice->mSrcOffset) / step_fixed + 1;
 
-						// avoid reading past the current buffer..
-						if (((writesamples * step_fixed + voice->mSrcOffset) >> FIXPOINT_FRAC_BITS) >= SAMPLE_GRANULARITY)
+						// avoid reading past the current buffer: drop the last frame
+						// only when it lands on the next block's first sample
+						if ((((writesamples - 1) * step_fixed + voice->mSrcOffset) >> FIXPOINT_FRAC_BITS) >= SAMPLE_GRANULARITY)
 							writesamples--;
 					}
 
